			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				176,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Deps/Editor): Sync Microsoft pointer to 87a1679c with Phase 10.5 Claude lifecycle\n\nAdvance the Microsoft VS Code Editor dependency submodule from c9f9e54d to 87a1679c (upstream 47e0dc55) to integrate the next phase of agent host improvements.\n\nKey upstream changes incorporated:\n- Agent Host Phase 10 & 10.5: Collapse provisional/session dual-map into a single ClaudeAgentSession identity, retire ClaudeMaterializer, and wire workbench client tools through an in-process MCP server for Claude sessions.\n- Sessions Management: Clean up ISessionsProvider chat API with a createNewChat/sendRequest two-step contract, refactor workspace picker for folder URIs, and add multi-provider session type pickers with per-agent icons.\n- MCP Enhancements: Allowlist openable URIs, escape command arguments for Windows, fix hover rendering.\n- Checkpoint Service: Integrate git operations (capture working tree, commit, ref management) with agent host session lifecycle.\n- BYOK Air-Gapped: Enable BYOK in environments without GitHub authentication.\n- Plugin System: Support git-subdir marketplace source kind for monorepos, persist installed plugin identity across reloads.\n- Bug Fixes: Handle corrupted session files gracefully, fix terminal resize guard during disposal, resolve symlink resolution in editFileToolUtils, guard splice(indexOf) against -1.\n\nNo source changes in the Land application — pure submodule pointer update to keep the dependency tree at the latest upstream.\n\nRefs: microsoft/vscode",
			"SHA": "ff6a6bc2298c965dc2422bca05ca4ac90d021d72"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T08:31:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				176,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Deps): Bump Microsoft and Tauri submodule pointers\n\nAdvance the Microsoft dependency submodule to incorporate the latest VS Code Editor upstream fixes (submodule pointer sync + typo fix in README marketplace description). Advance the Tauri dependency submodule to v2.11.2, bringing in Android build toolchain fixes, Tao 0.35.2, Wry 0.55.1, Brotli content encoding support, and the full plugin suite security patches.\n\nNo source changes in the Land application — pure submodule pointer updates to keep the dependency tree current.\n\nRefs: tauri-apps/tauri, microsoft/vscode",
			"SHA": "4ecfadfdbc76a0b097b67d2c7845caa5140bfdfe"
